  Fire rains down from all directions, the swarm seeking to bury us beneath weight of numbers, but our transcendent speed plucks us from danger again and again.

  Never once do I feel the burn of dragon's breath, and the margin of error only grows wider as we familiarize ourselves with our newfound power.

  Still, it's not enough to shake them completely, and I won't want them at my back when I face my true enemy.

//　勝つとなると、やはりこの数の差は軽視し難い。
//　一騎一騎墜としていてはいつ終わるか。
  How do I neutralize this threat? Knock them from the sky one by one? No. They still have an overwhelming numerical advantage. I'll run out of energy first.

//　いや、途中で力尽きる。

